  $ standing -= 2
  $ secrecy += 1
  He nods, slowly. He does not seem surprised. "I thought that you would say that," he says. "I had been afraid that you would say it more kindly." He turns the decanter a quarter of a turn on the table. "You will be neither my weapon nor my enemy, then, and I shall be able to keep you so for some little while. It is the one thing that I cannot promise to do for the others." He smiles, a very small smile, as if at an old jest. "The door is at the foot of the stair. You will find that it has been left open."
-> dawn

# price
:the_price
"Naturally," says the Prince. He is not offended. He has a gift for treating a price as a compliment. "It is a sign that the thing is taken seriously. What is it that you would like?"
* A seat at the council, at your left hand
  $ b3.price = "seat"
  $ standing += 3
  $ defiance -= 1
  He is silent for a moment. Then he says that it is a very great deal to ask, and that it is quite fair, and that the chair is kept. You think of the council of the court as you saw it that evening, the sixty beautiful faces, and you do not entirely like what you have bought. It is a seat in a house with no exits.
* The house in the rue Saint-Jacques is not to be touched. Not by the court, not by the Prince's friends
  $ b3.price = "valere"
  $ loyalty.keepers += 3
  $ bond.adelaide += 1
  He looks at you for a long time. "I did not know that you had such a household," he says, at last. "I shall see to it. It will be known in every house of the court by Sunday." He writes a line, on a leaf of the book that he had on his knee, and signs it, with his full name, and a title that has not been used in France since Catherine's day. It is a thing that no one has ever got from him before. It is a very thin piece of paper, and you are well aware of how thin.
* Nothing from the court. Only that you tell me, honestly, what the Prince does not tell his council
  $ b3.price = "roll"
  $ cunning_brutal -= 2
  $ secrecy += 1
  The Prince laughs, for the first time, a low dry sound with no breath in it. "You have taken the one thing that I could not refuse," he says. "I should like to say that I am sorry. I find that I am not." He gives you his hand. It is as cold and light as a dry leaf. "Then we shall be friends, Monsieur, for as long as I can bear it."
* Say that you will think about the price, and take the commission in the morning
  $ b3.price = "none"
  $ cunning_brutal += 1
  "Ah," says Gualtiero, softly. "That is the oldest of all the prices." He inclines his head. "I will wait. It is a thing I am good at." He does not seem displeased. He looks, for a moment, like a man who has been told that a very difficult game is still to be played.
